Description: allow pinned directory generations to converge on branch removal
 An inotify watch can keep a directory inode alive after its dentry is
 reclaimed. A later branch add may create a second generation of the same
 merged directory; branch removal can then make both generations converge on
 one surviving lower inode. Keep one directory generation hashed and leave an
 extra pinned generation unhashed, while preserving the fail-closed collision
 guard for non-directories.
Author: MiniOS Linux Team <crims0n@minios.dev>
Forwarded: https://github.com/fulalas/aufs-ng/pull/1
Last-Update: 2026-09-04

